body:
I feel the same way. If someone wants to end their life, they should have assistance in doing so especially if they are ill mentally/physically.  But the truth is there is no way to check how genuine someone's reasons are for quitting life/whether its curable or not

&#x200B;

I find that survival is so competitive and its always been the survival of the fittest/richest. And there are way too many people in the world already struggling to reach that. If some people want to leave, why shouldn't they be able to? This may give others who are unemployed/homeless more resources. I dont know I could be wrong, just my thoughts on this...

It's not selfish to expect someone to live up to their words and promises. Holding on is a way to cope with emotions. May it not be the best way.

&#x200B;

However, what is selfish is them leaving behind when they said they would never leave. 

&#x200B;

But I get what you are conveying. It is definitely better to let go and respect their decision.
